## two_modules_one_name (exit 1)
error[Z0107]: `share_missing` is defined in both `functions/clean.zeff` and `functions/tidy.zeff`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:1
  |
2 | use functions::tidy
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ brings in `share_missing` again
  |
  = help: write the one meant in full: `clean::share_missing(...)` or `tidy::share_missing(...)`

## script_and_module (exit 1)
error[Z0107]: `quadruple` is a function of this script and of `functions/clean.zeff`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | use functions::clean
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ brings in `quadruple` again
...
3 | fn quadruple(x: Float) -> Float { x }
  |    --------- the script's
  |
  = help: write the one meant in full: `functions::quadruple(...)` for the script's, `clean::quadruple(...)` for the module's

## statement_in_module (exit 1)
error[Z0323]: a module file holds `///` text, `fn` definitions and `use` lines only
 --> functions/odd.zeff:7:1
  |
7 | let k = 2
  | ^^^^^^^^^ a statement in a module
  |
  = help: move the statement to a script in `scripts/`; a module's functions take what they need as arguments

## module_named_like_a_package (exit 1)
error[Z0323]: a module may not be named `data`, the name of a package
 --> functions/data.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | /// Share of rows where a variable is missing.
  | ^ the file's name
  |
  = help: rename the file; `data::f` names the package's function

## module_name_not_a_name (exit 1)
error[Z0323]: `functions/bad name.zeff` is not a name a module can have
 --> functions/bad name.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | /// Share of rows where a variable is missing.
  | ^ the file's name
  |
  = help: name the file in snake_case, as `clean_wages.zeff`, since `use functions::clean_wages` names it (section 3.6)

## incomplete_page (exit 1)
error[Z0319]: the page of `half` in functions/bare.zeff is incomplete: it lacks `x:` and its meaning, `returns:` and what the value holds, one example, a line `> statement` with its output under it
 --> functions/bare.zeff:2:4
  |
2 | fn half(x: Float) -> Float { x / 2 }
  |    ^^^^ a module function without its complete page
  |
  = help: a function in `functions/` carries its page in `///` lines: the summary, a description, `name: text` for each parameter, `returns:`, and `> statement` examples with their output (section 9.1 of the Engine and Project Specification)

